# ============================================================================
# DebateKit n8n Community Node — Local Development
# ============================================================================
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS:
#   Local dev config for building / linking the n8n community node
#   (`n8n-nodes-debatekit-ai`). Used when running a local n8n instance and
#   pointing it at this in-progress node build.
#
#   The node itself does NOT read environment variables at runtime — users
#   configure their DebateKit API key via the n8n "DebateKit API" credential
#   UI inside their own n8n instance.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   Then fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# RUNNING LOCALLY:
#   1. `bun run build` (or `npm run build`) compiles the node to dist/
#   2. Point your local n8n at this directory via N8N_CUSTOM_EXTENSIONS below
#   3. Restart n8n; the DebateKit nodes appear in the node palette
# ============================================================================


# ============================================================================
# N8N LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
# ============================================================================

# Absolute path to this `integrations/n8n` directory.
# n8n loads compiled custom nodes from this path on startup.
# Example: /Users/you/Desktop/projects/roundtable-dashboard/integrations/n8n
N8N_CUSTOM_EXTENSIONS=/absolute/path/to/roundtable-dashboard/integrations/n8n
